#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Add four opt-in global-alloc and sched2 rules, first needed by func_L04_0040AD28.

-frac2-ga-no-lo-sum-pref: in set_preference a LO_SUM source gives its destination no register
preference (so none is passed on by expand_preferences).
-frac2-ga-divisor-first: a pseudo set once from a const_int (REG_EQUIV) and used as a DIV, MOD,
UDIV or UMOD divisor is allocated before all other pseudos.
-frac2-sched2-call-copy-fp-wait: after reload, no floating-point load (from memory or of a
constant) issues in the same cycle as a copy that saves a call's value register in a call-saved
register right after the call.
-frac2-sched2-const-low-reg-first: on a full sched2 tie between two constant loads into hard
registers, the lower-numbered register goes first.

Forced on for every USA v1.01 C unit they change 211, 48, 69 and 986 functions: opt-in per-unit
models under the owner's standard of 12 November 2026. Default compilation is unchanged.

Usage: l04_ad28_rules.py <gcc directory>
"""
